 160:Generated_Source\PSoC6/BLE.c **** * Function Name: Cy_BLE_Stop
 161:Generated_Source\PSoC6/BLE.c **** ***************************************************************************//**
 162:Generated_Source\PSoC6/BLE.c **** * 
 163:Generated_Source\PSoC6/BLE.c **** *  This function stops any ongoing operation in the BLE Stack and forces the 
 164:Generated_Source\PSoC6/BLE.c **** *  BLE Stack to shut down. The only function that can be called after calling
 165:Generated_Source\PSoC6/BLE.c **** *  this function is Cy_BLE_Start() when Cy_BLE_GetState() API returns 
 166:Generated_Source\PSoC6/BLE.c **** *  CY_BLE_STATE_STOPPED state. 
 167:Generated_Source\PSoC6/BLE.c **** *
 168:Generated_Source\PSoC6/BLE.c **** *  Calling this function results in generation of 
 169:Generated_Source\PSoC6/BLE.c **** *  a CY_BLE_EVT_STACK_SHUTDOWN_COMPLETE event on a successful stack shutdown.
 170:Generated_Source\PSoC6/BLE.c **** * 
 171:Generated_Source\PSoC6/BLE.c **** * \return
 172:Generated_Source\PSoC6/BLE.c **** *  cy_en_ble_api_result_t : Return value indicates if the function succeeded or
 173:Generated_Source\PSoC6/BLE.c **** *  failed. Following are the possible error codes.
 174:Generated_Source\PSoC6/BLE.c **** *
 175:Generated_Source\PSoC6/BLE.c **** *    Errors codes                    | Description
 176:Generated_Source\PSoC6/BLE.c **** *    ------------                    | -----------
 177:Generated_Source\PSoC6/BLE.c **** *    CY_BLE_SUCCESS                  | On successful operation.
 178:Generated_Source\PSoC6/BLE.c **** *    CY_BLE_ERROR_INVALID_OPERATION  | On calling Cy_BLE_Stop before calling Cy_BLE_Start.
 179:Generated_Source\PSoC6/BLE.c **** *
 180:Generated_Source\PSoC6/BLE.c **** ******************************************************************************/
